    "text": "(i) Ice formed by heavy water sinks in normal water due to higher density of  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>  than normal water<br/><br/>(ii)  <math><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mover accent=\"false\"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></mover><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> <br/><br/>(iii) Water can show amphiprotic nature and hence water can act both as an acid a base<br/><br/>(iv) There is extensive intermolecular hydrogen bonding in the condensed phase instead of intramolecular H-bonding",
